  "reasoning": "Statewide Cook PVI lists New York at D+8, indicating the state votes about eight points more Democratic than the national average in recent presidential elections.[1] Recent-cycle searches show no competitive 2026 federal statewide races (no Senate race and no gubernatorial race on the ballot in 2026), so the best quantitative baseline is New York\u2019s recent presidential performance, such as 2016 when Democrats won 59% to 36.5%\u2014a margin of roughly 23 points.[14] With a structurally Democratic PVI and consistent double\u2011digit Democratic presidential margins, and no evidence of current-cycle statewide federal polling that suggests a major realignment, New York\u2019s current federal-election partisan lean is strongly Democratic.[1][14]",
